# SSH: willowchromebook-penguin

Crostini Linux on the Chromebook that runs `m2000-monitor.service`. Reachable over **Tailscale**, not LAN mDNS.

| | |
|---|---|
| Tailscale name | `willowchromebook-penguin` |
| Tailscale IP | `100.69.70.24` |
| SSH port | **2222** (port 22 is closed) |
| User | `shibiao` |
| Auth | Mac `~/.ssh/id_rsa` (BatchMode works from the Mac) |

```bash
ssh -p 2222 -o BatchMode=yes shibiao@100.69.70.24
```

Also: `willowchromebook-penguin.tail0eb5c4.ts.net` (use `-p 2222`). If connecting via Kali as a jump, still use port 2222 on the Chromebook; Kali itself is `ssh kali` (192.168.86.51).

Service path / logs:

```bash
# on penguin
systemctl --user status m2000-monitor.service
journalctl --user -u m2000-monitor.service --since "7 days ago"
```

Code on device: `/home/shibiao/m2000_keepalive/`
